From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000038
Subject: [PATCH] Mod hooks and shell guilds: what a mod's script can do with ambient shells

The core side of the mod hooks in population_engine (search "RAGNAROKMAC (mod hooks)" and
"RAGNAROKMAC (shell guilds)"):

- Script commands (src/custom/script.inc): population_face, population_respawn,
  population_revive, population_death_event, population_chat_event, population_chatroom,
  population_chatroom_close, population_guild, population_guild_join, population_guild_leave,
  population_guild_ally, population_war.
- Battle config: population_engine_respawn_min_ms / _max_ms / _skew (how long a dead ambient
  shell lies; 5000/5000/1 is the old fixed 5 s), population_engine_no_kill_steal (0),
  population_engine_shell_kill_events (1: a shell that breaks the Emperium runs the castle's
  OnAgitBreak like a player; 0 drops it as before; 2 every monster's death event).
- clif.cpp: public chat reaches population_engine_on_public_chat (the mod's chat event).
- Shell guilds live only in the map server's memory, at guild ids 1900000001-1900009999:
  guild.cpp never asks the char server about them, never sends it their member or chat
  packets, and runs castle scripts' pending info events once the mod makes the guild. A
  castle a shell guild takes is saved to the char server as unowned (it stays theirs in
  this map server); a mod that wants it kept across a restart remembers it and sets it again.
- battle.cpp: for a shell at war (population_war), the engine's per-map shell "party" id
  (0x70000000 | map) no longer makes it an ally of every other shell on a PvP or GvG map;
  it fights by guild like a player. Shells not at war are as before.
- pc.cpp: a shell at war that dies on a PvP or GvG map goes through the engine's own death
  handling (the mod's death event, its respawn delay) instead of rAthena's return to the
  save point. Shells not at war are as before.

